#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# ramanujan_tau

#% text
# `ramanujan_tau(n)` gives the Ramanujan tau function, the coefficient of `q^n` in `q` times the product of `(1 - q^k)^24`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `tau` is multiplicative, with `tau(p^(k + 1)) = tau(p)*tau(p^k) - p^11*tau(p^(k - 1))` for primes `p`; `tau(1)` is 1.

#% item
# `ramanujan_tau` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
ramanujan_tau(1)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
ramanujan_tau(2)
#% output
#= -24

#% cell
ramanujan_tau(range(10))
#% output
#= [1, -24, 252, -1472, 4830, -6048, -16744, 84480, -113643, -115920]

#% cell
ramanujan_tau(1000)
#% output
#= -30328412970240000

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# Multiplicativity:

#% cell
[ramanujan_tau(6), ramanujan_tau(2)*ramanujan_tau(3)]
#% output
#= [-6048, -6048]

#% text
# Deligne's bound `abs(tau(p)) <= 2*p^(11/2)`:

#% cell
n(abs(ramanujan_tau(97))/(2*97^(11/2)))
#% output
#= 0.4434710683210847

